C++20 std::erase_if on std::vector<int>.

With the member-typedef conformance fix ([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef]) symex
executes the REAL std::vector / erase_if machinery (no truncation), and the
resulting size assertion is verified soundly within resources.
See doc/architectural/cpp-class-template-instantiation-plan.md.
